 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.1,
   "dur": 5.757,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Do your nerve cells touch? Mostly, no. For decades, no microscope could show it."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 6.7,
   "dur": 8.039,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Your brain holds over a hundred trillion meeting points: over ten thousand for every person alive. Through a lens, they look joined."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 15.5,
   "dur": 10.379,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Camillo Golgi, who made the stain, saw one continuous web. With it, Santiago Ramón y Cajal saw separate cells. In nineteen oh six they shared a Nobel, still arguing."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 26.7,
   "dur": 12.922,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "In the nineteen fifties, electron microscopes finally showed it: a gap. At most junctions, electricity can't jump it. Calcium floods the tip, tiny sacs spill a chemical messenger, and it drifts across."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 42.7,
   "dur": 7.772,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "The handoff takes about a thousandth of a second. Use a junction, and it can grow stronger: likely part of how you learn."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 54.3,
   "dur": 5.22,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "So your nerve cells mostly don't touch. They talk, across gaps, in chemicals."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 60.3,
   "dur": 7.335,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Meanwhile, as you watched, you took about fifteen breaths. Each started at the base of your brain and crossed gaps like these."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 68.7,
   "dur": 3.762,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: those breaths. Where does all that air go?"
  }
 ]
}